
Day - 42
--------

	TestNG - Test New Generation
	Java based unit testing tool.
	
	Advantages:
	-----------
	
	1) Test cases and test suits
	2) Grouping of test cases
	3) Prioritize
	4) Parameterized
	5) Parallel testing 
	6) Reports
	
	
	TestNG Configuration
	--------------------
	
	1) Install TestNG in eclipse from marketplace (Mandatory)
	2) Add testng library to build path/ add testng dependency in pom.xml
	
	
	@Test - annotation
	
	1) TestNG execute test methods based on alphabetical order.
	2) @Test(priority=num) controls the order of execution.
	3) Once you provide the priority to the methods, the order of the method is not consider. 
	4) Priority can be random numbers (no need to have consecutive numbers)
	5) If you don't provide priority then default value is zero (0). This will execute before prioritized methods
	6) If the priority are same then it will execute in alphabetical order.
	7) Negative numbers are also allowed in priority.
	8) TestNG execute methods only if they are having @Test Annotation.
	
	
	execute testcase using testng xml file
	
	testng xml file
	---------------
	
	1) It created automatically
	2) It can be created manually
	
	 
	
	Annotations
	
	@Test
	
	@BeforeMethod
	@AfterMethod
	
	@BeforeClass
	@AfterClass
	
	@BeforeTest
	@AfterTest
	
	@BeforeSuite
	@AfterSuite
	
	
	TC1
	----
	
	1) Login  ------- @BeforeMethod
	2) Search ------- @Test
	3) Logout ------- @AfterMethod
	4) Login
	5) Adv Search --- @Test
	6) Logout
	
	
	
	
	
	
	
	
	
	